# Cross Encoder Rerankers and Query Expansion with an LLM

Neural reranking and rank fusion on the TREC Deep Learning 2019 passage task, plus an evaluation of whether LLM based query expansion actually improves retrieval.

## Overview

This project builds a two stage retrieval pipeline: a first stage retriever followed by cross encoder reranking, evaluated on the **TREC Deep Learning 2019** passage ranking task. It then combines multiple rerankers using rank fusion, and separately tests a popular idea — using an LLM to rewrite or expand the query before retrieval — to see whether it earns its added complexity.

The headline finding is a negative result: **LLM based query expansion degraded retrieval quality relative to the plain query.** Fusing several weaker rerankers, by contrast, outperformed the single best model. Both results point the same way: a technique should prove its contribution before being trusted in a pipeline.

